Generate a basic custom properties implementation for a specified target class inside of a specified package.
This is the starting point for onboarding new custom properties implementations in the codebase.

Usage:
  bin/rails g custom_properties_implementation --target-class TARGET_CLASS_NAME --database-cluster DATABASE_CLUSTER --package PACKAGE_NAME

Required Options:
  --target-class      Class name that the custom property data will be associated with (e.g., Repository, Organization)
  --database-cluster  Database cluster name where the custom property tables will be hosted (e.g., Repositories, Users)
  --package           Packages folder name where the implementation should be placed (e.g., repositories, orgs, users)

Optional Options:
  --skip-sorbet-rbi   Skip generating Sorbet RBI files with bin/tapioca dsl
  --skip-packwerk     Skip updating Packwerk todo list with bin/packwerk update-todo
  --skip-migration    Skip running database migrations with bin/rails db:migrate
  --verbose           Show verbose output from executed commands

Examples:
  bin/rails g custom_properties_implementation --target-class Repository --database-cluster Repositories --package repositories
  bin/rails g custom_properties_implementation --target-class User --database-cluster Users --package users --verbose
  bin/rails g custom_properties_implementation --target-class Organization --database-cluster Main --package orgs --skip-sorbet-rbi
  bin/rails g custom_properties_implementation --target-class Project --database-cluster Repositories --package repositories --skip-migration

This generator creates:
  - A definition model file: packages/{package}/app/models/{target-class.underscore}_custom_property_definition.rb
  - A value model file: packages/{package}/app/models/{target-class.underscore}_custom_property_value.rb
  - A properties config file: packages/{package}/app/models/{target-class.underscore}_properties_config.rb
  - A custom properties dependency file: packages/{package}/app/models/{target-class.underscore}/custom_properties_dependency.rb
  - A domain accessor file: packages/{package}/app/public/{package}/domain/custom_properties.rb
  - A domain registration file: packages/{package}/app/public/{package}.rb (if it doesn't exist)
  - A domain file: packages/{package}/app/public/{package}/domain.rb (if it doesn't exist, or updates existing)
  - A domain accessor test file: packages/{package}/test/public/{package}/domain/custom_properties_test.rb
  - A definition test file: packages/{package}/test/models/{target-class.underscore}_custom_property_definition_test.rb
  - A value test file: packages/{package}/test/models/{target-class.underscore}_custom_property_value_test.rb
  - A factory file: test/factories/{target-class.underscore}_custom_properties_factories.rb
  - A definition migration file: db/migrate/{timestamp}_create_{target-class.underscore}_custom_property_definitions.rb
  - A value migration file: db/migrate/{timestamp}_create_{target-class.underscore}_custom_property_values.rb
  - Automatically adds packages/custom_properties to packages/{package}/package.yml dependencies
  - Automatically adds required database dependency to packages/{package}/package.yml external_dependencies
  - Automatically adds the CustomPropertiesDependency include to the target class file (if it exists)
  - Automatically creates necessary directory structures if they don't exist
  - Automatically adds the generated table names to the appropriate database cluster table list in lib/github/database_structure.rb
  - Optionally runs database migrations (unless --skip-migration is specified)
  - Optionally generates Sorbet RBI files (unless --skip-sorbet-rbi is specified)
  - Optionally updates Packwerk todo list (unless --skip-packwerk is specified)

The generated definition model will include the CustomProperties::DefinitionBase module and follow
the same pattern as existing custom property definitions like OrganizationCustomPropertyDefinition.

The generated value model will include the CustomProperties::ValueBase module and follow
the same pattern as existing custom property values like OrganizationCustomPropertyValue.

The generated properties config will implement the ICustomPropertiesConfig interface and provide
access to the generated definition and value model classes, following the same pattern as
OrganizationPropertiesConfig and RepoPropertiesConfig.

The generated domain accessor will include the CustomProperties::DomainAccessorBase module and provide a feature_enabled? method, following the same pattern as existing domain accessors like Orgs::Domain::CustomProperties and Repositories::Domain::CustomProperties.

The generated domain registration file will extend GH::Domain::Registration and register the package's domain class, following the same pattern as existing packages like packages/releases/app/public/releases.rb. If this file already exists and contains the proper registration, it will not be modified.

The generated custom properties dependency file will be included in the target class to provide custom property methods and interfaces, following the same pattern as existing dependencies like Repository::CustomPropertiesDependency.

The generated test files will follow the same testing patterns as existing custom property tests,
including comprehensive test coverage for validation, instrumentation, and business logic.

The generated factory file will provide FactoryBot factories for both the definition and value models, following the same patterns as existing custom property factories like organization_custom_properties_factories.rb.

The generated migrations will create tables with the same structure as existing custom property tables
like organization_custom_property_definitions and organization_custom_property_values but named
for the specified target class and configured for the specified database cluster.
